{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199376-mage-ronin-revenent-and-fomorus-crossover-and-logic-behind-it","id":1199376,"title":"Mage, Ronin, Revenent and Fomorus - Crossover and logic behind it","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-25T08:09:08-07:00","id":1199376,"title":"Mage, Ronin, Revenent and Fomorus - Crossover and logic behind it","content":"Here's the idea. A rich and powerful Ventrue Elder wants control of a city. He feels like to get an edge on the competition he needs some forces which act as Unknowns. The other Elders know Kindred too well to be defeated through conventional means, so he decides to put out feelers for unusual supernatural creatures who he can employ and control.<br /> <br /> I feel like a Ronin, Revenent, Fomorus and Mage would be fitting choices.<br /> <br /> Revenent gets the protection of a powerful domitor, and can increase their Discipline levels above 1.<br /> <br /> Fomorus is addicted to a Pentex product which has been discontinued, and thanks to the Contacts and Resources of the Elder he can have as much as he wants, for a price. This serum keeps him young and strong, and is the source of his Powers.<br /> <br /> Ronin is disillusioned from the Garou, since the only Tribe they tried to join rejected them. They're young and carefree, and getting to do a job where their curse is valued, exalted, is amazing. Plus he can live in luxury in his early 20s, as long as he does the odd job for his employer.<br /> <br /> Mage... I'm drawing a blank. I can't see why a Mage would work for a Vampire, and how the power balance would work between them. What could a Mage really, really need? Money doesn't feel like a compelling answer for me. Mages can make money themselves after all, one way or another. Perhaps the Ventrue is in control of a powerful Mage-related item, and working for them allows them access to the book/relic/whatever.<br /> <br /> Questions for the forum:<br /> <br /> - How would you work power balance in such a case? Our Ronin is stuck with level 1 gifts, our Revenent has high EXP prices, and our Fomorus and Mage can spend their EXP quite efficiently to gain power.<br /> <br /> - What would strengthen their motivations to work for such an individual?<br /> <br /> - How would they work together? And what would a Kindred need them for? What do they bring to the table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T09:37:10-07:00","id":1199397,"title":"","content":"If the Ventrue is careful and clever enough not to get backstabbed this could be the edge he needs to perform a coup well above his station.<br /> <br /> Depends on the mage, they would love things like an information network, maybe the Ventrue gets info from Nosferatu and fellow clansmen that the Mage needs to find some arcane secret or an edge on its own enemies. Or the Vampire agrees to help the mage with mortal backup for their own mission. Money is useful, depending on the mage they too wouldn't mind a legal cushy paycheck and nice apartment. You could also have the Ventrue get the Mage's family into excellent schools or jobs. Not all mages can do everything, most can't and can only do some things, so there are a lot of things singular mages could want. You could even give the mages vampire blood, or permanently assign a ghoul to help the mage. Maybe even help the mage start up a cult of acolytes and help them find newly awakened. An up and coming young mage wouldn't mind making friends with the new prince of a city after all. Few can counter the Technocracy bureaucratically like a Ventrue Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T09:55:58-07:00","id":1199402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199376-mage-ronin-revenent-and-fomorus-crossover-and-logic-behind-it#post1199376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Mage... I'm drawing a blank. I can't see why a Mage would work for a Vampire, and how the power balance would work between them. What could a Mage really, really need? Money doesn't feel like a compelling answer for me. Mages can make money themselves after all, one way or another. Perhaps the Ventrue is in control of a powerful Mage-related item, and working for them allows them access to the book/relic/whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of mercenary Mages. As of M20 Ventrue can buy Technocracy Surplus. This is before you get into all the things Mages can do with Money. I'm going to suggest a syndicate mage working to set the Ventrue's influence up into Primal Ventures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Questions for the forum:<br /> <br /> - How would you work power balance in such a case? Our Ronin is stuck with level 1 gifts, our Revenent has high EXP prices, and our Fomorus and Mage can spend their EXP quite efficiently to gain power. </div> </div> </div>They aren't. Its like trying to Balance a Ghoul with a Elder. Both are perfectly playable concepts both have theirown books built on it. They are not meant to play together. I'd suggest Trouping out. Let people play 3ish characters(1 Mage, 1 Revenant/Ghoul, 1 Formor/Ronin)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - What would strengthen their motivations to work for such an individual? </div> </div> </div><br /> Greed is a wonderful motivator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - How would they work together? And what would a Kindred need them for? What do they bring to the table? </div> </div> </div>Everything on this list can do a pretty good job of &quot;go out during the day and murder kindred in their havens&quot; the Ronin also is pretty good at doing that at night. Mages of course bring all sorts of out of context problems to the table. Ghouls/Revnants bring the same thing to the table they always have and Formori are pretty versitile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T11:28:05-07:00","id":1199431,"title":"","content":"I would suggest also Sorcerers and or Psychics, and they probably work better being ghouled too. But Revenants are somewhat familiar to vampires, well less so in modern Camarilla I suppose. If you get a sorcerer you can also fund them and try to get them to teach more sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T14:45:43-07:00","id":1199482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199376-mage-ronin-revenent-and-fomorus-crossover-and-logic-behind-it?p=1199431#post1199431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest also Sorcerers and or Psychics, and they probably work better being ghouled too. But Revenants are somewhat familiar to vampires, well less so in modern Camarilla I suppose. If you get a sorcerer you can also fund them and try to get them to teach more sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! A Psychic would be a great addition. They were being examined by a facility which got gutted in funding cuts, and fell into the hands of one of this Ventrue's ghouls. I mean what Prince doesn't want a pet mortal who can move objects with her eyes?<br /> <br /> - Mage who is trying to stun his fellow Awakened in the Traditions by forming an information and resources network which rivals those built over decades in a few month's work. Furthermore, the Elder has a stockpile of items that are of interest to the Traditions. A strange weapon confiscated from a Technocrat, some texts on spirits recovered from the collection of a Sabbat Priest, reports on the movements of Technocratic agents...<br /> <br /> - Revenent or Dhampir with Vampire-style EXP and raised caps thanks to the Ventrue's blood. The idea is that this ghoul is a total prodigy, hence them being included in such a group. Furthermore thanks to the Blood Bond they are actually loyal to the Elder and will regulate the others in the party somewhat<br /> <br /> - Ronin with a Rank-free Gifts system, they just need to justify which Gifts they acquire. They're working for the Elder since they feel like their Curse is actually valued in this line of work, and since it means he can live in a suite in a fancy hotel (a nice change from living on the street because your Rage alienates strangers)<br /> <br /> - Psychic who was recruited by a Pentex subsidiary and turned into a Fomorus. Furious at her mistreatment, she had a psychic meltdown and destroyed the facility, contributing to the decline of the daughter company. In the aftermath she was &quot;acquired&quot; by the Prince and given an offer she can't refuse; specialist treatment to deal with the malevolent force inside of her, along with access to lots of goodies seized from the fallen company (including a serum she needs to stay young and focus her powers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-25-2018, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:43:01-07:00","id":1199512,"title":"","content":"Building on the relationship between the Ronin and the Ventrue...<br /> <br /> Our Ronin grows up as a ward of the state. Mother in jail, father off the scene, and becomes homeless at 15. He learns to live with the fact that society has rejected him, and that &quot;good&quot; people will look the other way when it suits them. He's got a hunger, and he survives by begging and stealing.<br /> <br /> At 16, he goes through the First Change. His newborn Rage alienates the few friends he has, and he is lost until Garou find him. Finally, he might belong. Glass Walkers try to induct him, but the Totem rejects him and he is cast out. This only deepens his sense of rejection. He is now a pariah among what are meant to be his kin.<br /> <br /> Now 17, a hungry Ventrue with a taste for homeless blood attempts to chow down on what looks like a normal kine. Panicking, and mildly resistant to the Kiss, our Ronin takes wolf form and escapes. The shocked Ventrue reports the appearance of this homeless youth to his Sire...<br /> <br /> The Elder, upon meeting the Ronin, takes a genuine liking to him. He can see a real hunger and alienation in this young man. Seducing him with Presence and tempting him with expensive gifts, the Elder essentially establishes an asexual &quot;sugar dating&quot; situation with the young Werewolf. Storytelling this I would make it deeply uncomfortable. Never play down the fact that this young man has been rejected by society and the Garou nation, and that for the first time in his life he is fulfilled and supported, and not only that his curse is celebrated and treated as something special with this Ventrue... but at the same time don't shy away from the fact that a 150+ year old undead and manipulative man is controlling a 17 year old with money and intimacy and emotional control, both mundane and supernatural. Ideally it should challenge people.<br /> <br /> Our Ronin would be deeply defensive of the Elder, and have a total attachment complex. Terrified of rejection, terrified of failing the man he loves, terrified of being alone again. Generally scornful of society and &quot;good&quot; people, as he's been on the other side of things and seen all of society's ills, leaving him somewhat amoral. Easily stressed, and unfortunately prone to Frenzy. Being rejected by two societies and learning to cope with the curse alone has left him with a high Rage rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-25-2018, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T22:38:07-07:00","id":1199598,"title":"","content":"A fomor can rocket to extreme power by abandoning Autonomy or accumulating more Taints. It doesn't even require experience points to accomplish this, and, in fact, experience doesn't matter to possessed characters in Werewolf where their powers are concerned, except to raise tempers if they gain new ones, like Rage or Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T00:31:27-07:00","id":1199620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199376-mage-ronin-revenent-and-fomorus-crossover-and-logic-behind-it?p=1199598#post1199598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fomor can rocket to extreme power by abandoning Autonomy or accumulating more Taints. It doesn't even require experience points to accomplish this, and, in fact, experience doesn't matter to possessed characters in Werewolf where their powers are concerned, except to raise tempers if they gain new ones, like Rage or Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the Freak Legion rules. There, the only Taints you have are the ones you start with, and the ones you gain through Botches and specific Taints/Powers which can introduce new Taints.<br /> <br /> Powers are only raised by EXP.<br /> <br /> However, if you do gain a Taint, then the ST may award you EXP to make up for it, so there is power there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T01:36:40-07:00","id":1199637,"title":"","content":"Story Beats:<br /> <br /> Elder needs you to be incognito security (disguised as catering) at a classy business event. Keep his Ghoul alive, prevent interference from potential threats, protect the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Elder needs the 4 team members to trawl through all of the articles seized from the compound where the Psychic was &quot;acquired&quot;. Unfortunately there are still some dangerous living inventory within the storage, like a pack of Warwolves (Pentex experiment, they are like Garou but mindless and only have Crinos and Wolf forms). A Black Team sent by a Pentex branch arrives to claim inventory and destroy anything dangerous halfway through. The idea is to tie the Psychic's backstory into a session so people get to know them.<br /> <br /> Elder needs the team to deal with a problematic group of Garou who are interfering with the Camarilla's business, and his own. This pack includes some Garou who were present when the Ronin failed the rite to enter a tribe.<br /> <br /> The Dhampir/Revenent tries to discover their origin, as they don't know the identity of their mother (who is either a thinblood or a revenent). They cash in a favour the Elder owes them from a previous session to get the information they need, and the help of the others. The path to discovering what happened to their mother leads them through some dangerous scenarios, naturally.<br /> <br /> The Prince has placed a bounty on a pack of infernalist kindred, who include a member of the illustrious Red List. The Elder tries to handle the situation so he can claim some hefty boons. Among the infernalists is a Nephandus who the Mage has encountered before, who represents a toxic and subverted version of the Mage's paradigm.<br /> <br /> As a finale, the Elder is killed by a rival Kindred after being betrayed and outmaneuvered, leaving his coterie of &quot;peculiars&quot; high and dry. Do they just aim to escape with their lives? Do they stick together? Or do they try and take over all of the wealth and power their employer had collected, by force?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-26-2018, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T21:42:31-07:00","id":1199943,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Mage working with the Ventrue<br /> - An elder Ventrue would probably have the skills to know how to manipulate someone without disciplines; to work out what someone wants and what they are willing to do for it. It could be completely mercenary.<br /> - There could also be the network of information and contacts available from the Ventrue.<br /> - The Ventrue can accomplish things that would attract paradox for the mage when it comes to outright manipulation of emotions and minds of people.<br /> - How about a demolition order for an opposing tradition's Chantry?<br /> <br /> But, what about more Vampire related things? Maybe an Order of Hermes Tradition Mage wants to take a fight to the Tremere Clan, or steal their knowledge and see if there is a way to use their Magic (Thaumaturgy) in a way that it isn't powered by blood, but is still immune to Paradox?<br /> <br /> Lastly, A Vampire can create Tass very easily (Vitae) from regular blood, and it just takes a little prime to rip it out instead of ingesting it and becoming blood bound","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T23:50:13-07:00","id":1199956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199376-mage-ronin-revenent-and-fomorus-crossover-and-logic-behind-it?p=1199943#post1199943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Mage working with the Ventrue<br /> - An elder Ventrue would probably have the skills to know how to manipulate someone without disciplines; to work out what someone wants and what they are willing to do for it. It could be completely mercenary.<br /> - There could also be the network of information and contacts available from the Ventrue.<br /> - The Ventrue can accomplish things that would attract paradox for the mage when it comes to outright manipulation of emotions and minds of people.<br /> - How about a demolition order for an opposing tradition's Chantry?<br /> <br /> But, what about more Vampire related things? Maybe an Order of Hermes Tradition Mage wants to take a fight to the Tremere Clan, or steal their knowledge and see if there is a way to use their Magic (Thaumaturgy) in a way that it isn't powered by blood, but is still immune to Paradox?<br /> <br /> Lastly, A Vampire can create Tass very easily (Vitae) from regular blood, and it just takes a little prime to rip it out instead of ingesting it and becoming blood bound</div> </div> </div> </div>Great ideas. A source of Quintessence is something I didn't think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}